From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Omer Katz <omerkatz@chromium.org>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 10:12:28 +0200
Subject: [cppgc] Update the Steele-style barrier to always retrace

The barrier retraced objects only if they were already marked. This
doesn't work well with concurrent marking because the object could be
marked and the main thread hasn't observed it yet. Instead change the
barrier to mark regardless of whether the object was already marked.

Bug: 575143870
Change-Id: I5f027c5c5c28cc23fc25d562d266081afe216dc1
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/v8/v8/+/8614239
Reviewed-by: Michael Lippautz <mlippautz@chromium.org>
Commit-Queue: Omer Katz <omerkatz@chromium.org>
Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#111098}

Electron adaptation notes (43-x-y):
- src/heap/cppgc-internal/marker.h does not exist on V8 15.0; the same
  MarkerBase::WriteBarrierForObject() lives in src/heap/cppgc/marker.h,
  so the hunk is applied there. No other changes.

